      "content": "I see. So you're saying the technical points are valid in a vacuum, but they're being weaponized politically? That's a pretty strong take. \n\nIf I'm writing this for my readers, I need to be careful about how I frame the \"legitimacy\" of their side. From your perspective, is there any actual merit to the opposing view's core philosophy—the idea that we shouldn't force these transitions through mandates and should instead let the market dictate the speed of change—or is that also just a way to stall?",
